\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar near low vs yen after China raises rates.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada  \par \uc2 633 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2004\par 09:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 29 (Reuters) - The dollar hovered near a six-month low against the yen on Friday on worries about the strength of the U.S. economy and the effect on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a rate rise in China.  \par \par \uc2 Markets were taken by surprise on Thursday when China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would raise rates, in an effort to cool its red-hot economy.  \par \par \uc2 The yen and commodity-exporting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Australia dollar initially sank on worries that slower Chinese growth would hurt their economies, giving the dollar a lift.  \par \par \uc2 But with analysts divided over which economy, including the the United States, would be hurt the most from a possible slowdown in China, many traders said it was too early to draw any conclusions.  \par \par \uc2 "The market doesn't know how this China issue will affect \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of the international bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  department at Daiwa Securities SMBC.  \par \par \uc2 Also under pressure from end-month selling by Japanese exporters, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as low as 105.97 yen, just above a six-month trough of 105.90 hit on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 It was at 106.09/12 yen at 0644 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The euro stayed in a tight range on Friday, trading at $1.2756 slightly higher compared with late U.S. levels.  \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, it hit an eight-month peak around $1.2840, less than a cent off a record high of 1.2930 scaled in February.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the low of 105.90 yen would likely be tested later on Friday, as many in the market were keen to challenge the resolve of Japanese policymakers, who are widely believed not to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since March.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures for October at 1000 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki reiterated on Friday that the authorities would act if \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved out of line with economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 CHINA IMPACT  \par \par \uc2 China increased in its benchmark one-year yuan lending rate to 5.58 percent from 5.31 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said that it was uncertain what impact the move would have on Beijing's timetable to increase the flexibility of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 China's yuan trades in a narrow band at around 8.28 to the dollar and is widely believed to be undervalued. Beijing has been under pressure from the United States and, increasingly, Europe, to adopt a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime.  \par \par \uc2 A revaluation would likely support the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 Traders were also keenly awaiting Tuesday's U.S. presidential election, with polls still showing a close race between President George W. Bush and Democratic challenger John Kerry.  \par \par \uc2 "I think you've got to look at the possibility that like last time we won't get a quick result, and if the process becomes drawn out and confused, people will likely sell the dollar," said Toru Umemoto, research associate at the Global Security Research Centre at Keio University.  \par \par \uc2 The centre is headed by former \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Eisuke Sakakibara, often dubbed "Mr Yen".  \par \par \uc2 "But whether Bush or Kerry wins, the outlook is for an economic slowdown and we can expect a weaker dollar," said Umemoto, who expects the dollar to challenge 100 yen and the euro to test $1.30 by year-end.  \par \par \uc2 More immediately, traders were awaiting U.S. third quarter gross domestic product and a consumer sentiment survey for October - both due later in the day - given worries about the U.S. economic outlook after a recent surge in oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 The yen hardly moved after the Bank of Japan's Policy Board decided to maintain its current monetary easing policy, as widely expected. (Additional reporting by David McMahon).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041029e0at0063p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
