\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar firms after strong Chicago PMI.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrea Ricci  \par \uc2 613 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2004\par 16:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 29 (Reuters) - The dollar firmed against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday after a strong reading on manufacturing in the U.S. Midwest helped offset weaker-than-expected national growth data.  \par \par \uc2 The Chicago Purchasing Management Index, a key gauge of factory activity in the central region of the country, rose to 68.5 in October from 61.9 in September.  \par \par \uc2 Among the components of the index, the production index was the highest since August 1950 and the new orders reading was the highest in two decades.  \par \par \uc2 "These numbers are remarkably good and should be dollar supportive," said Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Group in Chicago.  \par \par \uc2 "But ahead of the election, it is unlikely that we will see the dollar get too strong," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Americans go to the polls on Tuesday. The latest Reuters/Zogby opinion poll has President George W. Bush and challenger Sen. John Kerry in a dead heat.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.2724 , off 0.16 percent from Thursday and down from $1.2745 shortly ahead of the data.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar had eased earlier on disappointing U.S. growth data. Real gross domestic product rose 3.7 percent in the July through September quarter, a faster pace than the 3.3 percent registered in the prior three-month period but well short of the 4.2 percent clip forecast by economists.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the reaction to the Chicago PMI probably was muted because the producer of the index, the National Association of Purchasing Managers-Chicago, had sent it to clients via e-mail inadvertently late on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Shortly before the data release, the group would not confirm whether the data sent on Thursday were correct. In fact, they were.  \par \par \uc2 Consumer sentiment data, also released on Friday morning, were better than economists had forecast but still reflected a fall from the prior month. The University of Michigan final October sentiment index fell to 91.7 from 94.2 in September.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they did not expect the strong PMI data to support the dollar for long.  \par \par \uc2 "The overall sentiment on the dollar is still so bearish that people are looking for good news to sell on the bounce," said Ken Landon, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Mixed U.S. economic data. low interest rates, a widening current account gap and uncertainty ahead of the election have been weighing on the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 DOLLAR STAYS WEAK AGAINST YEN  \par \par \uc2 The PMI data were unable to give the dollar a lift against the yen. The dollar traded at 106.08 yen , down 0.15 percent in the session and barely changed from its level ahead of the Chicago data.  \par \par \uc2 In Japan, authorities appeared reluctant to step into the market despite the yen's decline, with many analysts arguing the coming U.S. election was keeping them at bay.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were not a risk to the economy. The dollar slipped to fresh six-month lows of 105.92 yen following Fukui's comments.  \par \par \uc2 Bob Lynch, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in New York, warned against getting taken in by rhetoric of Japanese policy-makers.  \par \par \uc2 "When they were \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the billions of dollars last year, the official rhetoric didn't match it. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves too fast, whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces it or not, they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the four weeks ended Oct. 27 despite the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Gertrude Chavez in New York).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041029e0at009ii\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
