\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF: No  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Between Sep 29 To Oct 27  \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2004\par 12:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese finance authorities stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for most of October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday, marking the seventh straight month of zero \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MOF said it conducted no yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the period from Sept. 29 to Oct. 27, despite the dollar having slid considerably over the past two weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback, which was trading above Y111.00 in early October, has recently dropped to six-month lows below Y106.00, due to investor concern over the outlook for the U.S. economy and uncertainty over the U.S. presidential election on Nov. 2. As of 1000 GMT Friday, it was trading around Y105.95.  \par \par \uc2 Friday's data confirm the MOF has remained out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since mid-March, when it abruptly ended an unprecedented 15-month yen-selling campaign to keep the buoyant yen from harming Japan's economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 But market players are growing increasingly wary of the possibility that Japanese authorities may soon resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar continues to slide.  \par \par \uc2 Top Japanese officials, including Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki, have recently warned \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Tokyo will take action if it feels that movements are too disruptive or are straying too far from economic fundamentals  \par \par \uc2 Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data covers trades which settle in October. As spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades are settled after two business days, some analysts have said that even if authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past two days, they won't need to disclose the action until data for November is released next month.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie [ 29-10-04 1001GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041029e0at000n2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
