\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Falls To 8-Mo Low Vs Euro; Flat Vs Yen -2  \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2004\par 22:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 Oct 26, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 The mounting dollar-bearish mood has put a spotlight on the question of whether and when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resume its dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a sharp yen rise from derailing the nation's export-reliant economic recovery. Some dollar bears believe the MOF won't be able to take action until the U.S. presidential election is over for fear of affecting its outcome. But Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities, says it's "too dangerous" to assume Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities won't act before or just after the election. "If it becomes absolutely necessary, the chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (being conducted at such timing) can't be ruled out," Ueno said. In trying to gauge the timing of possible MOF action, many analysts point to levels such as Y106.12, the average assumed rate of big manufacturers for the latter half of this fiscal year shown in the Bank of Japan's "tankan" survey, and Y105.00, where many exporters have set their annual dollar/yen forecasts. A more important level, however, may be this year's low of Y103.40, which was set March 31 despite the massive yen-selling campaign the MOF was conducting at that time, analysts say. "Unless the pace of the yen's rise becomes extremely fast, the MOF will resume its dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when the greenback approaches Y103.40," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase Bank of Tokyo. In any case, the MOF is expected to examine various factors, such as overseas and domestic economic developments, as well as corporate earnings and stock price movements, in deciding when to take action, if any, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie  \par \par \uc2 Copyright 2004 Dow Jones. All rights reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020041026e0aq0020u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
