\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Treasurys Dn Slightly In Quiet Tokyo Trade Before US Data-2-  \b0\par\par\uc2 486 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2004\par 07:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2004, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--U.S. Treasury prices fell slightly Tuesday on small-lot selling, including position-adjustments by a handful of foreigners, bond dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Trade was very thin because Japanese government bond, stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were quiet.  \par \par \uc2 Market players are reluctant to actively deal bonds ahead of the release of a series of economic data, such as the U.S. consumer confidence index and July-September gross domestic product figures, this week.  \par \par \uc2 Around 0400 GMT, the 10-year note was down 1/32 at 102 5/32 to yield 3.97%. The 30-year issue was also down 2/32 at 109 5/32 to yield 4.76%, while the two-year note was down 1/32 at 99 30/32 to yield 2.51%.  \par \par \uc2 'Prices seesawed through a combination of small-lots selling and bargain-hunting. But the market was quiet, reflecting small moves in other markets,' a senior bond trader at a foreign brokerage firm said.  \par \par \uc2 The trader said that market players are generally cautious about building short-positions because of fragile stock prices and stable inflation-related data.  \par \par \uc2 Another trader said that the biggest event for the market is the U.S. October jobs data due out Nov. 5.  \par \par \uc2 He added that market players are watching \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.  \par \par \uc2 There is speculation that the Bank of Japan at the request of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may conduct yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb a stronger yen.  \par \par \uc2 Treasury prices are supported by hopes that Japan would increase purchases of Treasurys if the BOJ conducts yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's life insurance companies are generally interested in buying Treasurys without hedging against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks if the yen appreciates against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 There are a number of other key economic indicators due out this week before the U.S. presidential election on Nov. 2. They include the employment cost index in the third quarter and durable good orders for September.  \par \par \uc2 The Conference Board is scheduled to release the consumer confidence index for October later today.  \par \par \uc2 Prices at 0400 GMT:  \par \par \uc2 2 1/2% 2-year 99 30/32 Dn 1/32 2.51%  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2 3/4%  3-year  100        Unchanged 2.72% \par    3 3/8%  5-year  100 19/32  Unchanged 3.23% \par    4 1/4% 10-year  102  5/32  Dn  1/32  3.97% \par    5 3/8% 30-year  109  5/32  Dn  2/32  4.76% \par    2-10-Yr Yield Spread: 146 BPS Vs 146 BPS \par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the Chicago Board of Trade, the December bond futures contract was at 114 11/32, unchanged from the previous session. The most heavily traded June Eurodollar contract on the Singapore Exchange was at 97.385, down from 97.425 at the Chicago close.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Hiroshi Inoue, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-9203; hiroshi.inoue@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020041026e0aq004bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
