\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  Speculation Emerges Again  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Vames and Laurence Norman  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 1,080 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2004\par 21:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The 'i-word' is making the rounds again.  \par \par \uc2 The yen has made substantial gains versus the dollar recently, prompting many in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to wonder if Japanese officials might soon start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , purchasing dollars and selling yen.  \par \par \uc2 The motivation, as it has been for Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as recently as the first quarter of this year, would be to stop a strong yen from derailing Japan's economic recovery and hurting the international competitiveness of Japanese exports. It is also a tool for working against markets that have become disorderly.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials fueled the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation overnight, with finance minister Sadakazu Tanigaki quoted by Reuters as saying the government was monitoring exchange rate movements "carefully."  \par \par \uc2 But while most analysts don't staunchly rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts on behalf of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they don't view it as an imminent risk. "So far the move has been very orderly, and I don't think it's the kind of action that would lead to any \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," from Japanese officials, said Tetsu Hisa Hayashi, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The `orderly' word is key in guessing when Japan might feel compelled to throw its actual - rather than just vocal - presence back into the markets. By far the most ardent practitioner of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  among the world's leading industrialized nations, it tends to take action if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements are too rapid and volatile, usually designed to slow the pace of a move. That's inherently a vague concept, although some analysts have tried to define as a drop by the dollar of about two yen in one day. This time, the dollar has been edging rather than sliding lower; it hasn't lost more than two yen in a single day since mid-March.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, analysts say the current situation is more a matter of broad dollar weakness, rather than strength in the yen. To that extent, Japanese monetary authorities might be less inclined to act since the broad trade-weighted value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't necessarily as high as its value versus the dollar might suggest, said Alan Ruskin, research director at 4Cast, an advisory firm based in, New York.  \par \par \uc2 Indeed, the yen has gained roughly 3.5% versus the dollar over the past 10 trading sessions, compared to a mere 0.7% rise versus the euro. The euro has gained 2.7% against the dollar during the same timeframe.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      Government At Ease? \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other factors within Japan's economy might also be making \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials more sanguine in the face of the falling dollar. Specifically, the Japanese stock market has slipped toward the bottom of its range in recent weeks as the dollar has fallen, but it hasn't necessarily broken down.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Say you start to see feedback between the yen and the stock market, and you see the Nikkei plunge," said Ruskin. "That would start to make \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seem a whole lot more likely."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indirectly, a stronger yen might also provide a bit of relief for the Japanese economy in the face of record high oil prices, which have been seen as a major threat to the fragile Japanese economic recovery. Because oil is priced globally in dollars, Japan can effectively get more oil for the same amount of yen as the dollar gets weaker.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taken together, those various factors may make the Japanese economy more insulated from its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , particularly since faith has grown in the sustainability of Japan's economic recovery.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nandita Singh, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  research analyst at JPMorgan in New York, said Japan's Tankan survey indicated exporters believe their profits will rise 30%-40% on the year, even if the the yen reaches Y106. That leads JPMorgan and others, to say the bar might merely have been raised a bit for the value of the yen at which Japanese officials would act.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the rounds of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2003 and the first quarter of 2004, Y105 was viewed by the markets as an unofficial trigger for Japanese officials to defend. Subsequent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, came at times when the yen was weaker than it is now. On March 16 - which ABN Amro cites as the last known date of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - officials entered the market when the dollar dipped to Y108.60, above the current Y107.40.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JP Morgan analysts reckon this time around, the risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will grow when the yen breaks Y103.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Politics Factor \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Politics - read the U.S. presidential election - is also seen reducing the chances of BoJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hayashi, at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi, said volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets ahead of the presidential election is to be expected, and that the current bout of dollar weakness is in large part due to uncertainty over the outcome of the election. He reckons the dollar will at least partially recover after the election. However, he sees more woes ahead since "the U.S. trade situation will not be quickly solved if either candidate wins the election."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bush administration is already fending off attacks from Democratic candidate Senator John Kerry, that the president hasn't been aggressive enough in pushing China to revalue the yuan, which is held in a very tight band against the dollar. Kerry accuses the Chinese government of "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulation." A revaluation would make Chinese exports less competitive and in theory, bolster U.S. manufacturers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Adding real Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulation to China's yuan policy in the days leading up to an extremely tight election would be a blow to Bush from a Japanese government that's been one of his closest foreign allies.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nick Bennenbroek, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Brown Brothers Harriman, said the political pressure reinforces the strong economic reasons for not pressing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  button.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Clearly the U.S. and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have a pretty good working relationship ... Just a couple of weeks ahead of an election, you wouldn't want to unnecessarily ruffle any feathers," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And the political effect may last beyond Nov. 2. If Kerry were to win, Japan may be reluctant to do anything to damage what, after Kerry's campaign accusations, could be an awkward bilateral relationship at the onset.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Steven Vames; Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-5063; steven.vames@dowjones.com [ 10-21-04 1527ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020041021e0al0003m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
