\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar drops as sentiment outweighs economic data.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Plumberg  \par \uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2004\par 21:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 21 (Reuters) - The dollar fell to new lows on Thursday as tepid prospects for the U.S. economy, widening deficits and uncertainty over the outcome of the presidential election combined to cast a shadow on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Bearish sentiment even outweighed Thursday's better-than-expected economic data, analysts said, as traders sent the dollar to its lowest level against the euro since late February, a four-month low versus the yen and an 11-year low against the Canadian dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar is a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is injured on domestic and external grounds," said Ashraf Laidi, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with MG Financial Group in New York.  \par \par \uc2 After August's and September's employment reports showed job growth fell short of expectations, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors learned that the U.S. trade gap hit its second-highest level ever in August and that U.S. financial assets may be losing their luster for foreign investors.  \par \par \uc2 "Tell me, where is the bright side?" asked Laidi.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday a Federal Reserve gauge of business activity in mid-Atlantic region surged to 28.5 in October, far higher than economists' predictions of an increase to 17.0.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fleetingly rose before quickly returning to levels reached before the report as a closer look showed a drop in both the employment and outlook components.  \par \par \uc2 "The (headline number) is stronger than expected. The six-month outlook has come back to temper that," said Lisa Finstrom, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with Citibank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The euro's convincing break above $1.2460 last Friday caused some analysts to take heed of warnings from Fed officials on the current account deficit, which hit a record in the second quarter.  \par \par \uc2 "You've got a combination of fundamental and technical factors, which is sending the dollar lower," said Alex Beuzelin, senior strategist at Ruesch International in Washington, D.C.  \par \par \uc2 By late afternoon in New York, the euro was up to $1.2623 , close to its intraday peak of $1.2651, its strongest since late February. It was also 3 cents away from its record high.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell around 0.4 percent to 1.2171 Swiss francs , having reached a nine-month low overnight of 1.2150 francs and close to a new eight-year low. The dollar was also off at 107.41 yen , a fresh four-month low.  \par \par \uc2 JAWBONING THE GREENBACK  \par \par \uc2 As the dollar sinks against the yen, speculation is rising on verbal or actual market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities, who have not bought dollars with yen since March.  \par \par \uc2 Vice Finance Minister Koichi Hosokawa said early Thursday his ministry would continue monitoring moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and take appropriate action if needed.  \par \par \uc2 There is also a growing sense that global policy-makers see a weaker dollar as fundamental to redressing the U.S. trade deficit and keeping the U.S. economy the prime mover of global growth.  \par \par \uc2 "The next stage is to start looking for any \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  remarks from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  or from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said MG Financial's Laidi.  \par \par \uc2 A stark message came on Oct. 7, when Dallas Fed President Robert McTeer said: "Over time, there's only one direction for the dollar to go - lower."  \par \par \uc2 Whether U.S. interest rates continue to rise also is critical for the dollar's direction. Rising rates tend to be a boon for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as they attract foreign investors seeking higher-yielding assets.  \par \par \uc2 Fed Governor Ben Bernanke said in a speech on Thursday that he still expects future interest rate hikes to proceed at a "measured" pace, supported by forthcoming economic data. (Additional reporting by Jamie McGeever and John Parry).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041021e0al00avv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
