\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For Oct. 5  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,801 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2004\par 11:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0900 GMT, along with items expected later in the day. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com or by phone on 65-6415-4020.  \par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG: Post-1997 price records are expected to be set at two Hong Kong government land sales for residential use in mid-October. ("=UPDATE: HK Land Sale Set To Fetch Post-1997 Record Price," ran at 0821 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA: A tearful President Megawati Sukarnoputri conceded defeat Tuesday in last month's elections, paving the way for the winner Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono to move ahead with economic reforms needed to restore investor confidence in the country. ("=INDONESIA ELECTION:Megawati Concedes Defeat In Pres Vote," ran at 0731 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 MANILA: The days of loose monetary policy in the Philippines may be numbered as inflation surges to a three-year high and strong exports threaten to further stoke domestic demand. ("=\b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  WATCH: Philippine Data Suggest Hike Coming," ran at 0725 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL: Milder-than-expected inflation in South Korea last month, along with further evidence of slowing exports and weak domestic demand, has provided the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a window of opportunity to boost the flagging economy with its second interest-rate cut this year, economists say. ("=PREVIEW: CPI, Weak Demand To Nudge Bank Of Korea To Ease," ran at 0731 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: The Bank of Japan will keep its ultra-loose monetary policy and short-term money rates near zero until at least mid 2006 despite the country's continuing economic recovery, analysts say. ("=BOJ Watch: Tighter Policy Delayed As Deflation Lingers," ran at 0851 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 CANBERRA: Prime Minister John Howard said Tuesday a re-elected conservative government would expand its counterterrorism strategy by setting up a joint training center for Australian spies and their counterparts in Southeast Asia and the Pacific. ("=UPDATE: Australia PM Wants Regional Spy Training Center," ran at 0607 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Since it stopped selling yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in March, the Japanese government has kept a low profile, at home and abroad, on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues. But that doesn't mean \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a thing of the past. ("=\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Asia: \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Lying Low, But Won't Abandon \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," ran at 0540 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: U.K. telephone company Vodafone Group Plc filed a Samurai bond shelf registration at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, documents filed at the ministry showed Tuesday. ("Vodafone Group Registers Samurai Bond Shelf At Japan MOF," ran at 0528 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI: Taiwan's consumer price index rose for the ninth month in a row in September, exceeding market forecasts due to the sharp increase in food and oil prices, the island's top government statistics agency said Tuesday.("DATA SNAP: Taiwan's Sep CPI Rise Above Market Forecasts," ran at 0819 GMT; DATA VIEW to run by around 1000 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY: Australia's services sector activity continued to strengthen in September, with a reading of the sector hitting its highest level since January. ("Australia PSI +1.4 Pts To 56.0 in Sept Vs Aug," ran at 2330 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL: Growth in South Korea's exports of information technology goods likely will be limited in the fourth quarter due to falling prices for mobile handsets and liquid crystal displays, the Ministry of Information and Communication said Tuesday. ("LCD,Handset Price Drop To Limit Korea 4Q IT Export Growth," ran at 0445 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 EQUITIES  \par \par \uc2 =ASIA IPO FOCUS: Hutchison Telecommunications International Ltd. cutting the price of its share offer won't be enough to attract strong investor demand as concerns over its earnings outlook outweigh the benefits of a cheaper offering, say fund managers. ("=ASIA IPO FOCUS:HK Hutchison Telecom Cuts IPO;Slow Demand," ran at 0736 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 PERTH: BHP Billiton Ltd. said Tuesday that it will buy back up to A$1.5 billion of its shares as the world's biggest mining company seeks to distribute windfall profits driven by China's soaring commodity imports. ("=UPDATE: BHP Billiton Plans US$1.1 Bln Share Buyback," ran at 0625 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON: Air New Zealand Ltd. Tuesday said Singapore Airlines Ltd. will sell its 6.3% stake in the New Zealand national carrier. (2nd UPDATE to run around 1000 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG: The institutional tranche of China Power International Development's initial public offering is about three times oversubscribed, a person familiar with the situation said. (ASIAN IPO FOCUS to run shortly)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Toppan Printing Co. will acquire all outstanding shares of DuPont Photomasks Inc. for about $650 million or Y71 billion, the two companies said Tuesday. ("Toppan Printing Buys US DuPont Photomasks For Y71 Bln," ran at 0647 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI: The Taiwan government will sell 7.5 million shares of Taiwan Cooperative Bank through an auction from Tuesday through Friday, a source familiar with the process said Tuesday. ("Taiwan Govt Selling 7.5M Taiwan Coop Shrs Tue-Fri -Source" ran at 0148 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 MAKUHARI, Japan: Top executives of Sony Corp. and Matsushita Electric Industrial Co. said Tuesday Japanese electronics firms are well-positioned to capitalize on global demand for networked audiovisual products. ("Japan Elec Co Execs Upbeat On Growing Digital Demand," ran at 0815 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Honda Motor Co. said Tuesday that it will join Toyota Motor Corp. and Nissan Motor Co. in developing software and networks that control car electronics parts. ("Honda To Join Toyota, Nissan In Automotive Elec Sys Devt," ran at 0845 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 =ASIAN STOCK FOCUS: Cosco Corp Singapore Ltd. has been a favored stock in recent weeks and could rise further following an acquisition that will lift earnings. ("=ASIAN STOCK FOCUS:Cosco Singapore A Buy On Acquisition," ran at 0401 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 NEW DELHI: India's Supreme Court Tuesday gave state-run broadcaster Prasar Bharti the rights to telecast a much-anticipated cricket series, thwarting the hopes of Zee Telefilms Ltd., which bid a record amount for the rights and was hoping to use the series as a launch pad for a sports channel. The interim order came after Zee, India's largest listed media company, filed a petition against a decision by the Board of Control for Cricket in India to withdraw telecast rights it originally gave to Zee. (UPDATE to run shortly)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Japan's Fair Trade Commission said Tuesday it has raided about 40 companies, including Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd., on suspicion of bid rigging for the construction of bridges for the transport ministry and local governments. ("Japan Fair Trade Commission Raids M'bishi Heavy, Others," ran at 0510 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 =Asian Stock Focus: As shares of Malaysia's Tenaga Nasional Bhd. hit a 2-1/2-year high last month, some investors bet the state-controlled power utility was starting an extended rally; volume surged to its highest levels in four years. But volume has since eased off and the stock has pulled back. Analysts say this underlines the challenges faced by Tenaga, including a MYR31.82 billion debt mountain and little chance of higher electricity rates in the next 12 months. ("=Asian Stock Focus: Analysts Aren't Energized By Tenaga," ran at 0809 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Aeon Co. said Tuesday that it posted record profits and revenue for the first half ended Aug. 20 partly due to strong contributions from group companies such as Aeon Credit Service Co. ("Japan's Aeon Keeps FY Group Net Pft Outlook At Y66B," ran at 0642 GMT; UPDATE to run shortly)  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON: Australia's Prime Infrastructure Group Tuesday kept its cash-and-bonds takeover bid for Powerco Ltd. alive after revising the terms of its offer. ("UPDATE: Prime Infrastructure Rescues Powerco Takeover Bid," ran at 2351 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Sharp Corp. said Tuesday it has developed the world's largest liquid crystal display panel television, one with a 65-inch screen. ("Sharp Unveils 65-Inch LCD Television, World's Largest," ran at 0601 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Syngenta SA expects to achieve steady growth in Japan, the second largest market in the world for chemicals that protect crops against insects, executives of the Swiss agrochemicals maker said Tuesday. ("Syngenta Expects Steady Growth In Japan Agro-Chem Market," ran at 0836 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON: New Zealand's Telecom Corp. said Tuesday it is seeking a High Court ruling on the meaning of some provisions of the Telecommunications Act. ("NZ Telecom Seeks Court Ruling On Telecommunications Act" ran at 1945 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA: Indonesian food maker PT Indofood Sukses Makmur said it plans to sell a stake in its flour mill division in the next few months to secure funds for debt reduction and business expansion. ("=INTERVIEW: Indonesia Indofood To Sell Stake In Bogasari," ran at 0809 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES  \par \par \uc2 PERTH: Shares in Woodside Petroleum Ltd. surged to a record high Tuesday, buoyed by the promise of a new oil discovery off the coast of Mauritania.("=UPDATE: Australia's Woodside Finds More Mauritania Oil," ran at 0744 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA: Indonesia's crude palm oil exports are expected to fall by 20% in the fourth quarter from the previous quarter due to increasing domestic demand ahead of year-end holidays, the chairman of the Indonesian Palm Oil Producers Association, or Gapki, said Tuesday. ("Indonesia 4Q Palm Oil Exports Seen Dn 20% VS 3Q," ran at 0740 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK: The Agricultural Futures Exchange of Thailand, or AFET, has introduced a series of measures including lower trading margins and extended trading hours to generate investor interest and boost liquidity, AFET President Napaporn Kurupasutachai told Dow Jones Newswires. ("=INTERVIEW: Thai Agri Exch Seeks More Investors To Up Vol," ran at 0826 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Japan's Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry is accelerating efforts to create infrastructure for trading emission rights of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases in a bid to cut pollution as laid out in the 1997 Kyoto Protocol. ("METI Pushes Gas Emission Rights Trade, Opposes Carbon Tax," ran at 0538 GMT) [ 05-10-04 0901GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE: Saudi Arabian Oil Co.'s announcement of its latest crude official selling prices for November loading is expected to lend cue to the OSPs of other key Gulf producers from Kuwait and Iran later this week. ("UPDATE: Saudi Ups Nov Extra Light, Cuts Heavy Crude OSPs," ran at 0326 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO: Nippon Oil Corp. Tuesday announced plans to restructure its lubricating oil production \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in an effort to reduce operating costs and strengthen its price competitiveness. ("Nippon Oil To Restructure Lubricating Oil Output Ops," ran at 0645 GMT)  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON: World prices for commodities produced by New Zealand hit another record high in September, but the run of rises may be coming to an end, ANZ said after releasing its World Commodity Price Index Tuesday. ("NZ Commodity Prices Rise Again In Sep, Nearing Peak -ANZ" ran at 1200 GMT) [ 05-10-04 0901GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 62550  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041005e0a5000dc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
