\par\par \b \uc2 Ex-MOF Mizoguchi: Expect  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkt To Stay Stable Near Term  \b0\par\par\uc2 680 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2004\par 07:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements have been stable and will likely remain so near-term given a lack of potentially market-moving factors, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's former top bureaucrat said Friday.  \par \par \uc2 While the twin U.S. current account and budget deficits are one dollar-bearish factor, the deficits will likely improve, former Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 He added that any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market impact from the U.S. presidential election in November is likely to be temporary.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't see any factor that would cause large moves" in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mizoguchi said. [ 17-09-04 0538GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 With exchange rates stable, Japanese authorities haven't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since ending a massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in mid-March, said Mizoguchi, who is now the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Center for International Finance.  \par \par \uc2 "But that doesn't mean \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are gone," for good, he said, adding that "if the market shows excess volatility or disorderly movements, there may naturally be instances that require \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 From January 2003 to March 2004, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  - under Mizoguchi - dumped an unprecedented Y35 trillion in the markets, mostly for dollars, in a grueling battle with yen buyers. Japan's foreign reserves - already the world's biggest - skyrocketed 76% over the 15 months to $826.58 billion in March.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi justified his decision to order the yen-selling spree, saying that it was "a necessary and inevitable measure" to keep speculators from driving up the yen, as an unwarranted yen rise would have exacerbated deflation.  \par \par \uc2 "U.S. authorities understood that Japan's government and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  were working hard to overcome deflation, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a result of that," Mizoguchi said, making his first public comments since leaving the MOF in July.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deflation-fighting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also conducted solely for the sake of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and not to help finance the U.S. current account deficit, as some have speculated, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. has never said that (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was helping finance their deficit, and I myself have never held that view," Mizoguchi said. He added he thus doesn't see any impact on U.S. financing from the fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buying dollars.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese is believed to have invested most of the dollars bought through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in U.S. Treasurys, which have been helping stabilize U.S. interest rates, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 As for the decision to exit \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, that was due in part to signs - such as strong gross domestic product growth in the October-December quarter - that Japan's economy was recovering, Mizoguchi said.  \par \par \uc2 Indications that market sentiment was shifting from extreme dollar-bearishness was also one factor that led to the end of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added.  \par \par \uc2 "It wasn't a policy to continue indefinitely, and it needed to be ended," he said.  \par \par \uc2 On China, Mizoguchi said it was natural for the Group of Seven industrialized nations to hold regular exchanges of views with Beijing, giving China's growing importance in the world economy.  \par \par \uc2 He declined to comment directly on whether China would attend the G7 meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors scheduled for early October in Washington, or on what they would likely discuss.  \par \par \uc2 But he said that deputies of China and the G7 have been meeting informally since last September, when they met on the sidelines of the G7 meeting in Dubai, and that they have been conducting frank exchanges of views.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi said he believes Chinese officials share the G7's view that a more flexible exchange rate system would be in China's interest, and that Beijing will likely work toward achieving such a system in the future.  \par \par \uc2 He added that it was unlikely China's economy would experience a "hard landing," due to various steps being taken by the government.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson [ 17-09-04 0724GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040917e09h0004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
