\par\par \b \uc2 Japan August Foreign Reserves $827.95B; Up $8.75B On Mo  \b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2004\par 01:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's foreign reserves rose by $8.75 billion in August from a month earlier to $827.95 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 It was the fourth straight month of rise.  \par \par \uc2 August's increase in Japan's reserves of convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights follows modest gains of $1.25 billion in July, $1.10 billion in June and $1.88 billion in May. Reserves dropped $11.61 billion in April, breaking a seven-month surge to record highs.  \par \par \uc2 In the first three months of the year, reserves skyrocketed by more than $150 billion as the MOF ordered massive dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise and protect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-driven economic rebound.  \par \par \uc2 But as the government abruptly ended its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in March, changes in reserves in following months have been moderate, swayed mainly by factors such as interest earned on the government's overseas assets. [ 06-09-04 2357GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 August's rise in reserves was in part due to lower U.S. interest rates pushing up U.S. Treasury prices, inflating the value of Japan's U.S. Treasury holdings, according to a MOF official.  \par \par \uc2 He added that the euro's rise against the dollar in the month also boosted the dollar-value of the government's euro-denominated assets.  \par \par \uc2 The euro, which started the month trading at $1.2059 in the Tokyo market, rose to a high of $1.2382 on Aug. 20, before falling to a low of $1.1987 on Aug. 30, according to MOF data.  \par \par \uc2 Interest income on Japan's overseas assets, which consist largely of U.S. Treasurys, also contributed to the on-month rise, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 As a result of the gains, Japan's reserves hit the highest figure on record in August, surpassing the previous record $826.58 billion marked in March.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves were also the highest in the world for the 57th straight month in June, the latest month for which comparable data is available, the ministry said.  \par \par \uc2 According to IMF data, which differ slightly from those issued by the MOF due to differences in gold evaluation methods, Japan had $809.5 billion in reserves as of June - far outstripping China, which was in second place with $464.1 billion as of May.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Shawn Schroter and Hugh Lawson [ 07-09-04 0030GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040906e096000v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
