\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  in June-MOF.   \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2004\par 12:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 30 (Reuters) - Japanese authorities refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in June to cap the yen's rise, the third consecutive month without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) data showed on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The MOF has stayed away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since March, after selling 14.83 trillion yen ($137 billion) in the first three months of the year to keep the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains in check.   \par \par \uc2 Since then, the yen has traded in a range spanning from a four-year high of 103.40 yen at the end of March to nearly 115 yen in mid-May. Late on Wednesday, it was trading around 108.74.   \par \par \uc2 While government officials regularly issue warnings to the markets that they are on the lookout for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, few analysts showed concern over yen selling by Japanese authorities in the immediate future.   \par \par \uc2 "There's always a possibility that they'll enter the market to smooth any rapid rise in the yen, but it doesn't seem like they are out to defend a particular level, which is the difference from its previous campaign," said Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan.   \par \par \uc2 Many pointed out that the yen's recent gains had been made on the strength of Japanese fundamentals, unlike the rally seen earlier in the year, which many market players said had been fueled by speculation.   \par \par \uc2 Most analysts said the MOF seemed comfortable with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels at the moment, and that its return to the market would require sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings.   \par \par \uc2 "I think if we see very sharp moves in the downside in the dollar/yen we might see some returning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because we know that MOF does look at positioning and near-term volatility," said Naomi Fink, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas.   \par \par \uc2 "So if we see a sharp move downwards and a simultaneous buildup in speculative positioning, then I wouldn't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 Last year, Japanese authorities poured 20 trillion yen into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a record for a single year. ($1=108.22 Yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040630e06u000yh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
