\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Slides To Intraday Lows After Weak US Data  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Tom Barkley  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 969 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2004\par 14:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar extended its overnight losses early Thursday in New York, hitting its weakest level against the yen in over two months, following the release of worse-than-expected U.S. manufacturing and employment figures.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , already rattled by explosions linked to terrorists in Turkey and Iraq, was sold off modestly across the board after a report showing that new orders for durable goods unexpectedly fell 1.6% in May following an upwardly revised 2.6% dropoff the month before. The consensus view was for a 1.2% gain.  \par \par \uc2 "This number is very disappointing and we will see some follow-through (Thursday)," said Joseph Barnea, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank Leumi in New York." The durable goods number should give the euro its best chance of trying $1.22 again today."  \par \par \uc2 Early Thursday, the dollar was at Y107.28, below Y108.55 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was trading around $1.2146, up from $1.2085, but was lower against the yen at Y130.31 compared with Y131.24. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar fell to CHF1.2447 from CHF1.2532 Wednesday, while sterling was little changed at $1.8159 versus $1.8166 after recovering from overnight weakness.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, weekly jobless claims jumped 13,000 in the week ended June 19 to a seasonally adjusted level of 349,000, versus expectations of an increase of 4,000.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell overnight on news that a small bomb had exploded in the street in front of a hotel in Ankara where President George W. Bush was expected to stay when he visits Turkey over the weekend for the NATO summit. Two police officers were injured in the blast.  \par \par \uc2 Another explosion in a residential area of Istanbul was reported just as New York trading was getting underway, though the news it didn't have much immediate impact on the market.  \par \par \uc2 But coupled with a series of attacks in Iraq overnight, which killed 69 people, the events have further inflamed fears of increasing violence as the U.S. prepares to hand over power to the Iraqi government next week.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading broadly lower, but the yen remained among the strongest performers. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to benefit from a heavy flow of investment into the country's stocks to participate in the economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 A 1.4% rise in the Nikkei 225 stock index helped push the dollar below Y108 for the first time since mid-April to as far as Y107.13 and the euro to a two-month low of Y130.09.  \par \par \uc2 Barnea predicted that broad-based dollar weakness against the yen will continue, rejecting recent rumors of imminent Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the yen from appreciating too quickly.  \par \par \uc2 "I do not see any line in the sand for Japan and the yen and expect the dollar to drop to Y105 in the medium term," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's slide toward Y107 proves that recent inability to slip through Y108.40 was based on commercial moves, not Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Barnea said. [ 06-24-04 0855ET ]  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has steadied a bit after the initial selloff in the wake of the durable goods data, but it remains vulnerable as investors fret about rising violence.  \par \par \uc2 Typical safe-haven plays have been among the main beneficiaries, with the dollar down nearly 1% against the Swiss franc and gold rising over 1.5% to above $402 a troy ounce.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, investors may make another attempt to send the yen below Y107, despite increasing wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 John McCarthy, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ING Capital Markets, said the dollar still looks heavy against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "Strength in the yen reflects a much better picture in Japan," he said. While Japanese monetary authorities will likely counter any major moves, "it's clear that they can allow for gradual yen strength," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was supported by a bigger-than-expected rise of 2.2% in the tertiary industry index in April, fueling speculation that the Bank of Japan's Tankan survey next week will show further improvement in business confidence.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed a net Y548.5 billion in positive flows in the latest weekly data, helped by foreign buying of stocks and net selling of foreign bonds by Japanese investors.  \par \par \uc2 Steven Englander, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclay's Capital in New York, said high yields on Japanese government bonds, strong Japanese equities and easing deflationary pressures should keep the yen strong.  \par \par \uc2 "Undoubtedly, (Japanese monetary authorities) would probably draw the line at Y106 by picking up the phone and making some noise," Englander said, but he added that "every indicator has been positive, so it's hard to justify a weak yen right now."  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, however, market participants don't expect much more fallout ahead of next week's Federal Open Market Committee Meeting, when monetary policy makers are widely expected to lift rates by 25 basis points in the first hike in four years.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think a great deal is going to happen ahead of the Fed meeting," said McCarthy, adding that the euro is likely to continue to trade "very violently" in its recent range between $1.2050 and $1.22.  \par \par \uc2 Englander agreed, saying that with little in the durable goods data or Friday's revision to first-quarter U.S. gross domestic product likely to alter rate-hike expectations, the euro probably won't top $1.22 in the near term.  \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Barkley, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4385  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     tom.barkley@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Steven C. Johnson contributed to this story.) [ 06-24-04 0950ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074 1863 28038 4164  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020040624e06o0001f\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\li